SUMMARY:All Rivers Spill Their Stories to the Sea @ WTW Wadebridge
DESCRIPTION:All Rivers Spill Their Stories to the Sea (1h 39min)\nDocumenta
 ry\n\nOn England’s North East coast\, where rivers\, heavy industry and th
 e sea have shaped lives for generations\, fisherman Stan Rennie is watchin
 g the world he knows disappear. His family have worked these waters for ge
 nerations. Then\, almost overnight\, thousands of dead crabs and lobsters 
 wash ashore\, and a community already living with uncertainty is pushed in
 to crisis. Teesside filmmaker Jeanie Finlay brings warmth\, wit and deep l
 ocal feeling to this David-and-Goliath story of environmental damage\, off
 icial evasions and working-class resilience. At its centre is Stan: funny\
 , stubborn\, vulnerable and increasingly determined to be heard.\n\nStarri
 ng: Stan Rennie\n\nFilm release at WTW Cinemas Wadebridge\nBook tickets: h
 ttps://wtwcinemas.co.uk/wadebridge/film/5769/all-rivers-spill-their-storie
 s-to-the-sea\n\nFilm details: https://evenwebb.github.io/wtw-cinemas/films
 /all-rivers-spill-their-stories-to-the-sea.html
LOCATION:WTW Cinemas Wadebridge
URL:https://wtwcinemas.co.uk/wadebridge/film/5769/all-rivers-spill-their-st
 ories-to-the-sea
SEQUENCE:0
END:VEVENT
